# BUGS

Duplicate ids and duplicate names are not refused; a name or an id finds the first line that has it.

Names are not checked for the characters Plan 9 excludes (`?`, `=`, `+`, `-` and `/`); only `:` and newline are impossible.

An entry stores numbers, so a user whose id changes, or whose line is deleted, leaves its files owned by a number no name has, or by whoever takes the number next.

The file is advisory until keyd (M10): a client names whom it attaches as.
